 "summary": "**Market summary, 2026-11-04 (previous session: 2026-11-03)**\n\nThe S&P 500 (SPY) rose 0.30% to 754.35, though it is down 1.99% over five days. The Nasdaq 100 (QQQ) gained 0.62%, while the Dow (DIA) fell 0.44%. Technology (XLK) led sectors with a 1.31% gain. Staples (XLP) fell 2.07% and materials (XLB) dropped 2.01%. Industrials (XLI) rose 0.95%. Gold (GLD) fell 0.66% and long Treasuries (TLT) fell 0.76%. Oil (USO) rose 0.83%, and the US dollar (UUP) edged up 0.17%.\n\nTop eligible gainers were BUUU (+28.4%) and AEHR (+26.5%). Top losers were SUPN (-32.9%) and STVN (-28.6%). Uber (UBER) was the most-mentioned ticker in news. It reported Q3 2026 gross bookings of $59.8B, up 20% year over year, and guided Q4 gross bookings to $63.25B\u2013$65.25B. CVS Health announced plans to split into two public companies by 2028. Avient raised its full-year adjusted EPS guidance.",
